rationale:
Split. The selected node is De Giorgi's structure theorem in Gauss–Green form; its supplied proof chains a dozen independent named results, each a substantial formalization, so one monolithic proof would be unmanageable. Each child is one of these results: Riesz representation of the perimeter functional (Simon Ch. 2, 2.1–2.2 and Ch. 1, 4.14); a.e. convergence of normal averages (4.2, Ch. 1, 3.23); De Giorgi's cut-off/upper-density estimates (4.3 (1), (3)–(6)); a Sobolev inequality for ζ·1_F (Sobolev step of 4.3, Ch. 2, 2.5); two-sided volume density bounds (4.3 (10)–(11)); BV compactness for sets (Ch. 2, 2.6); half-space rigidity (4.3 (8)–(9)); convergence of blow-ups to the half-space (4.3 ‡); the tangent measure H^m⌞ν^⊥ a.e. (4.3 †); density one and the cone condition from a flat tangent measure (Ch. 3, Remark 1.5(3)); the rectifiability criterion (Ch. 3, 1.6 ⇐); and the identification μ = H^m⌞B with approximate tangent planes (parent steps 5, 7, 8). Every child type uses only contract, SimonGMT and Mathlib vocabulary, with the Gauss–Green pair written as explicit hypotheses. Each carries a complete numbered proof extracted from the parent proof and Simon's printed text, with the errata applied (the minus sign in 4.1; the limit {x^{n+1} > λ} in (9)) and every rigour-only departure stated: C¹ instead of Lipschitz cut-offs, finite differences instead of d/dρ, and Borel uniformization instead of Egoroff. With the children, the parent's own proof is the step-9 assembly: take (μ, ν) from gauss_green_measure; apply tangent_measure_ae; apply measure_eq_hausdorff with its hypothesis (RD) instantiated by the parent's declared dependency Submission.codim1_rdo_rectifiable_ae_density_one (P := m+1, n := m); then rewrite with μ = μHE[m].restrict B. This assembly compiles in Lean against stubs of the children and the uncle. Dependencies are acyclic:
- volume_density_lower ← cutoff_estimates, sobolev_perimeter;
- blowup_halfspace ← cutoff_estimates, volume_density_lower, bv_compactness, halfspace_rigidity;
- tangent_measure_ae ← normal_average_ae, cutoff_estimates, blowup_halfspace;
- rectifiable_criterion ← flat_tangent_density;
- hausdorff_identification ← flat_tangent_density, rectifiable_criterion.
Splitting all twelve at depth 5 leaves one more level (max_depth 6) for the heaviest pieces: Riesz on the subspace D, BV compactness, Sobolev, the rectifiability criterion and the identification. No child re-proves another DAG node; rectifiable_density_one enters only as hypothesis (RD). An independent adversarial review found no false statement, proof gap or sign error. Its minor remarks have been incorporated: a Borel-version citation, a positive Sobolev constant, and self-contained cut-off, divergence and rescaling steps.
